{"title": "Sectional Mock #41 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>If (3<sup>x</sup>)(3<sup>y</sup>) = 27 and (16)<sup>x</sup> (4<sup>y</sup>) = 256 then find the value of x and y?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; (3<sup>x</sup>)(3<sup>y</sup>) = 27 &#2324;&#2352; (16)<sup>x</sup> (4<sup>y</sup>) = 256 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; x &#2324;&#2352; y &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["x = 1, y = 2", "x = 1, y = 3", "x = 3, y = 1", "x = 2, y = 1"], "options_hi": ["x = 1, y = 2", "x = 1, y = 3", "x = 3, y = 1", "x = 2, y = 1"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>3<sup>x+y</sup> = 3<sup>3</sup> and 4<sup>2x+y</sup> = 4<sup>4</sup></p><p>So, x+y = 3 and 2x+y = 4. On solving these equations, we get x=1, y=2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>3<sup>x+y</sup> = 3<sup>3</sup> and 4<sup>2x+y</sup> = 4<sup>4</sup></p><p>So, x+y = 3 and 2x+y = 4. On solving these equations, we get x=1, y=2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>How many numbers are there between 100 to 1000 which are divisible by both 5 and 11? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>100 &#2360;&#2375; 1000 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2379; 5 &#2324;&#2352; 11 &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["19", "16", "18", "17"], "options_hi": ["19", "16", "18", "17"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Number divisible of 5 and 11 both = 5 * 11 = 55</p><p>The number  -  110, 165, ........... 990</p><p>a<sub>n</sub> = a + (n  -  1) * d</p><p>990 = 110 + (n  -  1) * 55</p><p>880 = 55n  -  55</p><p>55n = 880 + 55</p><p>n = 935/55 = 17</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number divisible of 5 and 11 both = 5 * 11 = 55</p><p>The number  -  110, 165, ........... 990</p><p>a<sub>n</sub> = a + (n  -  1) * d</p><p>990 = 110 + (n  -  1) * 55</p><p>880 = 55n  -  55</p><p>55n = 880 + 55</p><p>n = 935/55 = 17</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Study the given pie charts carefully and answer the question that follows.</p><p><img width=685 height=340 id=\"Picture 32\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21073/image018.png\"></p><p>The expenditure on food in 2021 was what percentage of the expenditure on education in 2020?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2325;&#2366; &#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2325; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"685\" height=\"340\" id=\"Picture 32\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21073/image018.png\"></p><p>2021 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;, 2020 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2341;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["95%", "85%", "90%", "80%"], "options_hi": ["95%", "85%", "90%", "80%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Expenditure on food in 2021 = 20% of 1080000 = &#8377;216000</p><p>Expenditure on education in 2020 = 25% of 960000 = &#8377;240000</p><p>Required percent = (216000/240000) * 100</p><p>= 90%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Expenditure on food in 2021 = 20% of 1080000 = &#8377;216000</p><p>Expenditure on education in 2020 = 25% of 960000 = &#8377;240000</p><p>Required percent = (216000/240000) * 100</p><p>= 90%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the average of the following sets of numbers.</p><p>693, 456, 876, 532, 934, 691, 596, 398, 682</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p>693, 456, 876, 532, 934, 691, 596, 398, 682</p>", "options_en": ["550.50", "750.80", "650.89", "725.90"], "options_hi": ["550.50", "750.80", "650.89", "725.90"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Average = (693 + 456 + 876 + 532 + 934 + 691 + 596 + 398 + 682)/9</p><p>= 5858/9</p><p>= 650.89</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Average = (693 + 456 + 876 + 532 + 934 + 691 + 596 + 398 + 682)/9</p><p>= 5858/9</p><p>= 650.89</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">3(16<sup>3</sup> - 6<sup>3</sup>)", "q_hi": "<p><div>&nbsp;&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">3(16<sup>3</sup> - 6<sup>3</sup>)", "options_en": ["96", "98", "112", "108"], "options_hi": ["96", "98", "112", "108"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>we have the equation as:-</p><p>3(16<sup>3</sup>  -  6<sup>3</sup>)/(16<sup>2</sup> + 6<sup>2</sup> + Q) = 30</p><p>3(4096  -  216)/(292 + Q) = 30</p><p>3880=2920 + 10Q</p><p>960=10Q</p><p>Q=96</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>we have the equation as:-</p><p>3(16<sup>3</sup>  -  6<sup>3</sup>)/(16<sup>2</sup> + 6<sup>2</sup> + Q) = 30</p><p>3(4096  -  216)/(292 + Q) = 30</p><p>3880=2920 + 10Q</p><p>960=10Q</p><p>Q=96</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>A and B together can complete a task in 20 days, and B and C together can complete the same task in 30 days. If A alone takes half as many days as C alone to complete the task, how long will A, B, and C working together take to complete the task?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; 20 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2324;&#2352; B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 30 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; C &#2360;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["9 days", "10 days", "12 days", "15 days"], "options_hi": ["9 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "10 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "12 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "15 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let rA, rB, rC be rates (job/day). Given:</p><p>rA + rB = 1/20 .. (1)</p><p>rB + rC = 1/30 .. (2)</p><p>A alone takes half as many days as C alone &rarr; tA = 0.5 tC &rarr; 1/rA = 0.5(1/rC) &rarr; rA = 2rC .. (3)</p><p>Substitute (3) into (1): 2rC + rB = 1/20 &rarr; rB = 1/20  -  2rC .. (4)</p><p>Substitute (4) into (2): (1/20  -  2rC) + rC = 1/30 &rarr; 1/20  -  rC = 1/30</p><p>&rarr;  - rC = 1/30  -  1/20 = (2  -  3)/60 =  - 1/60 &rarr; rC = 1/60 job/day</p><p>Step 3: rA = 2rC = 2/60 = 1/30 job/day</p><p>rB = 1/20  -  2(1/60) = 3/60  -  2/60 = 1/60 job/day</p><p>Combined rate = rA + rB + rC = 1/30 + 1/60 + 1/60 = (2 + 1 + 1)/60 = 4/60 = 1/15 job/day</p><p>Time = 1 &div; (1/15) = 15 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let rA, rB, rC be rates (job/day). Given:</p><p>rA + rB = 1/20 .. (1)</p><p>rB + rC = 1/30 .. (2)</p><p>A alone takes half as many days as C alone &rarr; tA = 0.5 tC &rarr; 1/rA = 0.5(1/rC) &rarr; rA = 2rC .. (3)</p><p>Substitute (3) into (1): 2rC + rB = 1/20 &rarr; rB = 1/20  -  2rC .. (4)</p><p>Substitute (4) into (2): (1/20  -  2rC) + rC = 1/30 &rarr; 1/20  -  rC = 1/30</p><p>&rarr;  - rC = 1/30  -  1/20 = (2  -  3)/60 =  - 1/60 &rarr; rC = 1/60 job/day</p><p>Step 3: rA = 2rC = 2/60 = 1/30 job/day</p><p>rB = 1/20  -  2(1/60) = 3/60  -  2/60 = 1/60 job/day</p><p>Combined rate = rA + rB + rC = 1/30 + 1/60 + 1/60 = (2 + 1 + 1)/60 = 4/60 = 1/15 job/day</p><p>Time = 1 &div; (1/15) = 15 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>Sagar and Virat started a Dhaba. The investment of Sagar is 9/8th times of the investment of Virat and the share of profit of Sagar is 135% of the share of profit of Virat. If Sagar invested for 18 months, then for how much time period Virat invested the money?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2366;&#2327;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2335; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2338;&#2366;&#2348;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2360;&#2366;&#2327;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358;, &#2357;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2366; 9/8 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2366;&#2327;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366;, &#2357;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; 135% &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2366;&#2327;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; 18 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2335; &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["15 months", "12 months", "24 months", "20 months"], "options_hi": ["15 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375;", "12 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375;", "24 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375;", "20 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let Virat invested the money for m months.</p><p>So, ratio of profit of Sagar and Virat = 135: 100 = 27: 20</p><p>=&gt; (9 * 18): (8 * m) = 27: 20</p><p>=&gt; 9 * 18/(8 * m) = 27/20</p><p>=&gt; m = (9 * 18)/8 * 20/27</p><p>=&gt; m = 15 months</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let Virat invested the money for m months.</p><p>So, ratio of profit of Sagar and Virat = 135: 100 = 27: 20</p><p>=&gt; (9 * 18): (8 * m) = 27: 20</p><p>=&gt; 9 * 18/(8 * m) = 27/20</p><p>=&gt; m = (9 * 18)/8 * 20/27</p><p>=&gt; m = 15 months</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>A ladder of length 3.5 m just reaches the top of a wall. If the ladder makes an angle of 60<sup>o</sup> with the wall, then what is the height of the wall (in m)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>3.5 m &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2368;&#2338;&#2364;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2336;&#2368;&#2325; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2361;&#2369;&#2305;&#2330;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2368;&#2338;&#2364;&#2368; &#2342;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; 60&deg; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; (m &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1.75", "3.5&radic;3", "(7&radic;3)/4", "3.5/&radic;3"], "options_hi": ["1.75", "3.5&radic;3", "(7&radic;3)/4", "3.5/&radic;3"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=210 height=242 id=\"Picture 39\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20111/image107.jpg\"></p><p>Let the height of the wall = h m</p><p>cos 60&deg; =AB/AC</p><p>1/2 = h/3.5</p><p>h = 3.5/2</p><p>h = 1.75 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=210 height=242 id=\"Picture 39\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20111/image107.jpg\"></p><p>Let the height of the wall = h m</p><p>cos 60&deg; =AB/AC</p><p>1/2 = h/3.5</p><p>h = 3.5/2</p><p>h = 1.75 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 6 women can complete a work in 3 days, and 9 girls can complete the same work in 2 days, then find the time taken to complete the same work by 8 women and 6 girls?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 6 &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; 3 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; 9 &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2306; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; 2 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; 8 &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; 6 &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["3 days", "4 days", "6 days", "9/7 days"], "options_hi": ["3 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "4 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "6 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "9/7 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Work done by 6 women in 1 day = 1/3</p><p>So, work done by 8 women in 1 day = 8/(3 * 6) = 4/9</p><p>And work done by 9 girls in 1 day = &frac12;</p><p>And work done by 6 girls in 1 day = 6/(2 * 9) = 1/3</p><p>So, work done by 8 women and 6 girls together in 1 day = 4/9 + 1/3 = 7/9</p><p>So, required time = 9/7 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Work done by 6 women in 1 day = 1/3</p><p>So, work done by 8 women in 1 day = 8/(3 * 6) = 4/9</p><p>And work done by 9 girls in 1 day = &frac12;</p><p>And work done by 6 girls in 1 day = 6/(2 * 9) = 1/3</p><p>So, work done by 8 women and 6 girls together in 1 day = 4/9 + 1/3 = 7/9</p><p>So, required time = 9/7 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the greatest five  -  digit number which when divided by 3, 4, 6 and 15 leaves remainder of 1 in each case.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2306;&#2330; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2375; 3, 4, 6 &#2324;&#2352; 15 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1 &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2348;&#2330;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["99935", "99961", "99960", "99984"], "options_hi": ["99935", "99961", "99960", "99984"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Greatest 5  -  digit number = 99999</p><p>LCM of 3, 4, 6 and 15 = 60</p><p>99999 when divided by 60 leaves 39 as remainder</p><p>Required number = 99999  -  39 + 1 = 99961</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Greatest 5  -  digit number = 99999</p><p>LCM of 3, 4, 6 and 15 = 60</p><p>99999 when divided by 60 leaves 39 as remainder</p><p>Required number = 99999  -  39 + 1 = 99961</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the total surface area of the hemisphere is 462 cm<sup>2</sup> and the radius of the hemisphere is half the radius of the sphere, then find the total surface area of the sphere. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 462 cm<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["2398 cm<sup>2</sup>", "2354 cm<sup>2</sup>", "2464 cm<sup>2</sup>", "2332 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["2398 cm<sup>2</sup>", "2354 cm<sup>2</sup>", "2464 cm<sup>2</sup>", "2332 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>The total surface area of the hemisphere = 3&#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>462 = 3 * 22/7 * r<sup>2</sup></p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 462 * 7/66 </p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 49</p><p>r = 7 cm</p><p>Radius of sphere = 2 * 7 = 14 cm </p><p>Hence, the total surface area of the sphere = 4&#960;r<sup>2</sup> </p><p>= 4 * 22/7 * 14 * 14 </p><p>= 2464 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The total surface area of the hemisphere = 3&#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>462 = 3 * 22/7 * r<sup>2</sup></p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 462 * 7/66 </p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 49</p><p>r = 7 cm</p><p>Radius of sphere = 2 * 7 = 14 cm </p><p>Hence, the total surface area of the sphere = 4&#960;r<sup>2</sup> </p><p>= 4 * 22/7 * 14 * 14 </p><p>= 2464 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The largest number that can divide 147, 183 and 271 leaving remainders 11, 13 and 16, respectively, is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2379; 147, 183 &#2324;&#2352; 271 &#2325;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 11, 13 &#2324;&#2352; 16 &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2348;&#2330;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2357;&#2361; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["14", "17", "15", "16"], "options_hi": ["14", "17", "15", "16"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>147 - 11 = 136</p><p>183 - 13 = 170</p><p>271 - 16 = 255</p><p>Find GCD of 136, 170, 255</p><p>Factorize: 136 = 2<sup>3</sup> * 17, 170 = 2 * 5 * 17, 255 = 3 * 5 * 17</p><p>GCD = <b>17</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>147 - 11 = 136</p><p>183 - 13 = 170</p><p>271 - 16 = 255</p><p>Find GCD of 136, 170, 255</p><p>Factorize: 136 = 2<sup>3</sup> * 17, 170 = 2 * 5 * 17, 255 = 3 * 5 * 17</p><p>GCD = <b>17</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>The length of the shadow on the ground of a tall cell tower of height 32&radic;3 m is 96 m. What is the angle (in degrees) of elevation of the sun?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>32&radic;3 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375;&#2354; &#2335;&#2366;&#2357;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2364;&#2350;&#2368;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2331;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 96 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; (&#2337;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["90&deg;", "45&deg;", "30&deg;", "60&deg;"], "options_hi": ["90&deg;", "45&deg;", "30&deg;", "60&deg;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=166 height=110 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27478/image003.png\"></p><p>AB = Height of cell tower</p><p>BC = Shadow of tower</p><p>Let the angle be 'X'.</p><p>tan X = AB/BC</p><p>tan X = 32&radic;3/96</p><p>tan X = 1/&radic;3 = 30&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=166 height=110 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27478/image003.png\"></p><p>AB = Height of cell tower</p><p>BC = Shadow of tower</p><p>Let the angle be 'X'.</p><p>tan X = AB/BC</p><p>tan X = 32&radic;3/96</p><p>tan X = 1/&radic;3 = 30&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The length of a cylindrical wire is 200 m. If the volume of the wire is 3.08 m<sup>3</sup>, then find the radius of the wire.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2340;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 200 m &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2340;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; 3.08 m<sup>3 </sup>&#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["7 cm", "14 cm", "9 cm", "21 cm"], "options_hi": ["7 cm", "14 cm", "9 cm", "21 cm"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>h = 200m</p><p>Volume of the cylindrical wire = 3.08 m<sup>3</sup></p><p>&#928;r<sup>2</sup>h = 3.08 m<sup>3</sup></p><p><img width=23 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21013/image004.png\"> * r<sup>2</sup> * 200 = 3.08</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = <img width=63 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21013/image005.png\"></p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = <img width=69 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21013/image006.png\"></p><p>r = <img width=31 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21013/image007.png\"> m</p><p>r = 7 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>h = 200m</p><p>Volume of the cylindrical wire = 3.08 m<sup>3</sup></p><p>&#928;r<sup>2</sup>h = 3.08 m<sup>3</sup></p><p><img width=23 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21013/image004.png\"> * r<sup>2</sup> * 200 = 3.08</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = <img width=63 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21013/image005.png\"></p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = <img width=69 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21013/image006.png\"></p><p>r = <img width=31 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21013/image007.png\"> m</p><p>r = 7 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the first term of an arithmetic progression is 5 and common difference is 7 then find the 10<sup>th</sup> term of the series.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2339;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2366; &#2346;&#2342; 5 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 7 &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2360;&#2357;&#2366;&#2306; &#2346;&#2342; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["57", "68", "62", "55"], "options_hi": ["57", "68", "62", "55"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>10<sup>th</sup> term of the AP = a + 9d = 5 + 9 x 7 = 68</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>10<sup>th</sup> term of the AP = a + 9d = 5 + 9 x 7 = 68</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the volume of the prism is 2178&radic;3 cm3 and the side of the base of the prism is 22 cm, then find the height of the prism. The base of a right prism is an equilateral triangle</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; 2178&radic;3 cm3 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; 22 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["20 cm", "16 cm", "14 cm", "18 cm"], "options_hi": ["20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the height of the prism be h cm</p><p>The volume of the prism = Area of base * height</p><p>&radic;3/4 * 22 * 22 * h = 2178&radic;3</p><p>h = 18 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the height of the prism be h cm</p><p>The volume of the prism = Area of base * height</p><p>&radic;3/4 * 22 * 22 * h = 2178&radic;3</p><p>h = 18 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A dishonest dealer sells his goods at a 30% loss on the cost price but uses a faulty weight that weighs 18% less. His profit or loss percentage (rounded off to 2 decimal places) is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2312;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; 30% &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2379;&#2359;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2348;&#2366;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; 18% &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; (2 &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;) &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["14.63% loss", "16.67% loss", "16.67% profit", "14.63% profit"], "options_hi": ["14.63% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;", "16.67% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;", "16.67% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;", "14.63% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>30% = 3/10</p><p>C.P = 10, S.P = 7</p><p>Actual C.P = 10 * 82/100 = 8.2</p><p>Loss % = (C.P  -  S.P) * 1100/C.P</p><p>= (8.2  -  7) * 100/8.2</p><p>= 14.63%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>30% = 3/10</p><p>C.P = 10, S.P = 7</p><p>Actual C.P = 10 * 82/100 = 8.2</p><p>Loss % = (C.P  -  S.P) * 1100/C.P</p><p>= (8.2  -  7) * 100/8.2</p><p>= 14.63%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two lines PQ and RS are parallel; A and B are two points on the line PQ and O is any point on the line RS. If &#8736;PAO = 74&deg; and &#8736;QBO = 134&deg;, then find the measure of &#8736;AOB.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306; PQ &#2324;&#2352; RS &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;; &#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; PQ &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; O &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; RS &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376; | &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736;PAO = 74&deg; &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;QBO = 134&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;AOB &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;|</p>", "options_en": ["42&deg;", "28&deg;", "46&deg;", "38&deg;"], "options_hi": ["42&deg;", "28&deg;", "46&deg;", "38&deg;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=254 height=164 id=\"Picture 106\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11888/image020.png\"></p><p>&#8736;PAO = 74&deg;</p><p>&#8736;QBO = 134&deg;</p><p>&#8736;AOS = &#8736;PAO = 74&deg;</p><p>&#8736;BOR = &#8736;QBO = 134&deg;</p><p>&#8736;BOS = 180&deg;  -  &#8736;BOR = 180&deg;  -  134&deg; = 46&deg;</p><p>&#8736;AOS = &#8736;AOB + &#8736;BOS</p><p>74&deg; = &#8736;AOB + 46&deg;</p><p>&#8736;AOB = 28&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=254 height=164 id=\"Picture 106\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11888/image020.png\"></p><p>&#8736;PAO = 74&deg;</p><p>&#8736;QBO = 134&deg;</p><p>&#8736;AOS = &#8736;PAO = 74&deg;</p><p>&#8736;BOR = &#8736;QBO = 134&deg;</p><p>&#8736;BOS = 180&deg;  -  &#8736;BOR = 180&deg;  -  134&deg; = 46&deg;</p><p>&#8736;AOS = &#8736;AOB + &#8736;BOS</p><p>74&deg; = &#8736;AOB + 46&deg;</p><p>&#8736;AOB = 28&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a person invested Rs. 3200 in compound interest at a 30% rate of interest compounded annually for three years, then find the total amount received. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2344;&#2375; &#2352;&#2369;.3200 &#2325;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; 30% &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2343;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 7630.4", "Rs. 7830.4", "Rs. 7230.4", "Rs. 7030.4"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 7630.4", "&#2352;&#2369;. 7830.4", "&#2352;&#2369;. 7230.4", "&#2352;&#2369;. 7030.4"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Amount = C.I + Principal amount </p><p>30% = 3/10 </p><p>C.I = P (13<sup>T</sup>  -  10<sup>T</sup>)10<sup>T</sup> [13 = sum of numerator and denominator of 3/10 and T = Time]</p><p>= 3200 * (13<sup>3</sup>  -  10<sup>3</sup>)/10<sup>3</sup> </p><p>= 3200 * (2197  -  1000)/1000 </p><p>= Rs. 3830.4 </p><p>Amount = 3830.4 + 3200 = Rs. 7030.4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Amount = C.I + Principal amount </p><p>30% = 3/10 </p><p>C.I = P (13<sup>T</sup>  -  10<sup>T</sup>)10<sup>T</sup> [13 = sum of numerator and denominator of 3/10 and T = Time]</p><p>= 3200 * (13<sup>3</sup>  -  10<sup>3</sup>)/10<sup>3</sup> </p><p>= 3200 * (2197  -  1000)/1000 </p><p>= Rs. 3830.4 </p><p>Amount = 3830.4 + 3200 = Rs. 7030.4</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>An inlet pipe can fill a water storage tank in 11 hours and an outlet pipe can empty the completely filled tank in 15 hours. If both pipes opened simultaneously. The time taken to fill the empty tank (in hrs) is :</p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2311;&#2344;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2319;&#2325; &#2332;&#2354; &#2349;&#2306;&#2337;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; 11 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2313;&#2335;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2352;&#2375; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; 15 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; (&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;:", "options_en": ["45(1/2)", "41(1/4)", "49(3/4)", "40"], "options_hi": ["45(1/2)", "41(1/4)", "49(3/4)", "40"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Capacity of tank = LCM of 11 &amp; 15 = 165 units</p><p>Efficiency of inlet pipe = 165/11 = 15 units/hour</p><p>Efficiency of outlet pipe = 165/15 = 11 units/hour</p><p>Required time = 165/(15  -  11) = 41.25 or 41(1/4) hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Capacity of tank = LCM of 11 &amp; 15 = 165 units</p><p>Efficiency of inlet pipe = 165/11 = 15 units/hour</p><p>Efficiency of outlet pipe = 165/15 = 11 units/hour</p><p>Required time = 165/(15  -  11) = 41.25 or 41(1/4) hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>32 &#247; 16 - 5 &times; 2", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>32 &#247; 16 - 5 &times; 2", "options_en": ["4/3", "5/4", "3/4", "4/5"], "options_hi": ["4/3", "5/4", "3/4", "4/5"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img border=0 width=149 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21536/image034.png\"></p><p><img border=0 width=99 height=55 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21536/image035.png\"></p><p><img border=0 width=52 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21536/image036.png\"></p><p><img border=0 width=44 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21536/image037.png\"></p><p><img border=0 width=41 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21536/image038.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img border=0 width=149 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21536/image034.png\"></p><p><img border=0 width=99 height=55 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21536/image035.png\"></p><p><img border=0 width=52 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21536/image036.png\"></p><p><img border=0 width=44 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21536/image037.png\"></p><p><img border=0 width=41 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21536/image038.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 6tanA  -  2tan<sup>3</sup>A = 2&radic;3 - 6&radic;3tan<sup>2</sup>A, then find the value of tan 3A.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 6tanA - 2tan<sup>3</sup>A = 2&radic;3 - 6&radic;3tan<sup>2</sup>A &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; tan 3A &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["&radic;3", "1/&radic;3", "1", "0"], "options_hi": ["&radic;3", "1/&radic;3", "1", "0"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Given,</p><p>6tanA  -  2tan<sup>3</sup>A = 2&radic;3 - 6&radic;3tan<sup>2</sup>A</p><p>2(3tanA  -  tan<sup>3</sup>A) = 2&radic;3 (1  -  3tan<sup>2</sup>A)</p><p>(3tanA  -  tan<sup>3</sup>A)/ (1  -  3tan<sup>2</sup>A) = &radic;3</p><p>tan3A = &radic;3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given,</p><p>6tanA  -  2tan<sup>3</sup>A = 2&radic;3 - 6&radic;3tan<sup>2</sup>A</p><p>2(3tanA  -  tan<sup>3</sup>A) = 2&radic;3 (1  -  3tan<sup>2</sup>A)</p><p>(3tanA  -  tan<sup>3</sup>A)/ (1  -  3tan<sup>2</sup>A) = &radic;3</p><p>tan3A = &radic;3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>If one root of the equation 2x<sup>2</sup> + kx + m = 0 is 3 and (k<sup>2</sup> + m<sup>2</sup>  -  25<sup>2</sup>) =  - 15 such that m &gt; 0, then the other root is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; 2x<sup>2</sup> + kx + m = 0 &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; 3 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; (k<sup>2</sup> + m<sup>2</sup> - 25<sup>2</sup>) = - 15 &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367; m &gt; 0 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["7", "5", "7/2", "15/2"], "options_hi": ["7", "5", "7/2", "15/2"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>As 3 is a root, so x = 3</p><p>2x<sup>2</sup> + kx + m = 0</p><p>18 + 3k + m = 0</p><p>m =  - (18 + 3k) .. (i)</p><p>(k<sup>2</sup> + m<sup>2</sup>  -  25<sup>2</sup>) =  - 15</p><p>k<sup>2</sup> + m<sup>2 </sup>= 625  -  15 = 610</p><p>k<sup>2</sup> + (18 + 3k)<sup>2 </sup>= 610</p><p>k<sup>2</sup> + 324 + 108k + 9k<sup>2 </sup>= 610</p><p>10k<sup>2</sup> + 108k  -  286 = 0</p><p>5k<sup>2</sup> + 54k  -  143 = 0</p><p>k = 2.2 or  - 13</p><p>m =  - 24.6 or 21</p><p>As m &gt; 0, so k =  - 13 and m = 21</p><p>Hence, the equation is 2x<sup>2</sup>  -  13x + 21 = 0</p><p>So, solving we get that the other root is 7/2.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>As 3 is a root, so x = 3</p><p>2x<sup>2</sup> + kx + m = 0</p><p>18 + 3k + m = 0</p><p>m =  - (18 + 3k) .. (i)</p><p>(k<sup>2</sup> + m<sup>2</sup>  -  25<sup>2</sup>) =  - 15</p><p>k<sup>2</sup> + m<sup>2 </sup>= 625  -  15 = 610</p><p>k<sup>2</sup> + (18 + 3k)<sup>2 </sup>= 610</p><p>k<sup>2</sup> + 324 + 108k + 9k<sup>2 </sup>= 610</p><p>10k<sup>2</sup> + 108k  -  286 = 0</p><p>5k<sup>2</sup> + 54k  -  143 = 0</p><p>k = 2.2 or  - 13</p><p>m =  - 24.6 or 21</p><p>As m &gt; 0, so k =  - 13 and m = 21</p><p>Hence, the equation is 2x<sup>2</sup>  -  13x + 21 = 0</p><p>So, solving we get that the other root is 7/2.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>The digit in the unit's place of (918)<sup>204</sup>  -  (1234)<sup>77</sup> is - </p>", "q_hi": "<p>(918)<sup>204</sup> - (1234)<sup>77</sup> &#2325;&#2375; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376; - </p>", "options_en": ["9", "2", "1", "8"], "options_hi": ["9", "2", "1", "8"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>&bull; (918)<sup>204</sup> &rarr; last digit 8; cycle of 8 is [8,4,2,6]; 204/4 = 0 (remainder) &rarr; 8<sup>4</sup> = 6</p><p>&bull; (1234)<sup>77</sup> &rarr; last digit 4; cycle of 4 is [4,6]; 77/2 = 1 (remainder) &rarr; 4<sup>1</sup> = 4</p><p>&bull; Unit digit = 6  -  4 = 2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>&bull; (918)<sup>204</sup> &rarr; last digit 8; cycle of 8 is [8,4,2,6]; 204/4 = 0 (remainder) &rarr; 8<sup>4</sup> = 6</p><p>&bull; (1234)<sup>77</sup> &rarr; last digit 4; cycle of 4 is [4,6]; 77/2 = 1 (remainder) &rarr; 4<sup>1</sup> = 4</p><p>&bull; Unit digit = 6  -  4 = 2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>The average age of A, B and C is 20 years. Two years ago, the sum of the ages of A and B was 6 more than that of C. Find the present age of C.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; 20 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;, A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354;, C &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; 6 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2341;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; C &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["28 years", "29 years", "26 years", "25 years"], "options_hi": ["28 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "29 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "26 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "25 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Sum of present ages of A, B, and C = 20 * 3 = 60 years</p><p>A + B + C = 60 ........ (1)</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>(A  -  2) + (B  -  2) = (C  -  2) + 6</p><p>A + B = C + 8 ...... (2)</p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p>C + 8 + C = 60</p><p>C = 26 years</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sum of present ages of A, B, and C = 20 * 3 = 60 years</p><p>A + B + C = 60 ........ (1)</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>(A  -  2) + (B  -  2) = (C  -  2) + 6</p><p>A + B = C + 8 ...... (2)</p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p>C + 8 + C = 60</p><p>C = 26 years</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}]}